\subsubsection*{Conceptual Data Flows}

Content creators mint NFTs on the Kusama parachain, embedding rights metadata (e.g., expiration for subscriptions). Consumers interact via:

\begin{enumerate}
    \item \textbf{Subscription Flow:} User sends DOT/KSM; smart contract mints renewable NFT, schedules XCM for renewals.
    \item \textbf{PPV Flow:} On-demand payment unlocks temporary access; NFT burns post-view.
    \item \textbf{Purchase Flow:} Permanent NFT transfer; cross-chain via XCM to user's preferred chain.
\end{enumerate}

Fallback: If parachain resources spike, migrate logic to Asset Hub for on-demand coretime, ensuring continuity.

\subsubsection*{Design Patterns and Challenges}

\textbf{Patterns Employed:}

\begin{itemize}
    \item \textbf{Composable Design:} RMRK 2.0 allows NFTs to nest (e.g., PPV as child of subscription NFT), enhancing flexibility.
    \item \textbf{Cross-Chain Atomicity:} Scheduled XCM ensures fail-safe transfers, addressing G1 (interoperability gaps).
    \item \textbf{Scalability Layers:} Use Kusama's relay chain for consensus; offload storage to IPFS.
\end{itemize}

\textbf{Addressed Challenges (from Phase 1's 10 Documented):}

\begin{itemize}
    \item \textbf{C1: High Transaction Costs:} Mitigated by free parachain via Canary Chaos; batching XCM calls.
    \item \textbf{C2: User Onboarding Barriers:} Simplified via wallet integrations (e.g., Talisman).
    \item \textbf{C3: Rights Enforcement:} On-chain ACLs with off-chain oracles for content delivery.
    \item \textbf{C4: Cross-Chain Latency:} Scheduled XCM; actual latency to be measured during evaluation.
    \item \textbf{C5--C10:} Similar mappings, e.g., security via runtime upgrades.
\end{itemize}

\subsubsection*{Security and Scalability Considerations}

Security relies on Substrate's FRAME macros for audited pallets. Scalability will be measured via parachain optimisations; fallback to Asset Hub prevents bottlenecks. The evaluation phase will document achievable TPS and identify any performance constraints.

This conceptual design sets the foundation for prototyping, aligning with updated RO2 and RO3.

